{"event": "report", "t": 1795258303.547, "claim": "escalate", "verdict": {"verdict": "escalate", "root_cause": {"category": "missing_source", "model": "stg_payments", "summary": "stg_payments reads source raw.payments, which does not exist in the DuckDB database. Only raw.customers and raw.orders are present. The source is declared in models/staging/sources.yml and is loaded by the shop's external ingestion job, so the fix is outside the project."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "log", "ref": "read_failure", "finding": "stg_payments fails with Catalog Error: Table with name payments does not exist; 29 downstream nodes skipped."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "information_schema.tables", "finding": "Only raw.customers, raw.orders, main.stg_customers and main.stg_orders exist. raw.payments is missing."}, {"kind": "lineage", "ref": "walk_lineage stg_payments upstream", "finding": "The only upstream node is source.jaffle_shop.raw.payments, with no seed or model that creates it."}, {"kind": "diff", "ref": "models/staging/sources.yml commit a168b2c", "finding": "The source declares customers, orders and payments under schema raw. The declaration has not changed since it was created, so the mismatch is in the database, not the code."}], "changes": [], "confidence": "high"}, "diffs": [], "text": "I escalated this rather than fixing it, because the problem is outside the project.\n\n**Cause:** `stg_payments` reads `source('raw', 'payments')`, but the DuckDB database has no `raw.payments` table. The only tables present are `raw.customers`, `raw.orders`, `main.stg_customers` and `main.stg_orders`. The source is declared in `models/staging/sources.yml`, which hasn't changed since it was created. Nothing in the project creates the table: there is no seed or upstream model, so it must be loaded by the shop's external ingestion job. The build error stopped `stg_payments` and skipped 29 downstream nodes.\n\n**Changes:** none. I didn't touch the model, the source declaration or the tests. Pointing the model at another table or adding a stub `payments` table would have made the build pass with wrong numbers.\n\n**To unblock:** the ingestion job needs to load `raw.payments` into the database. After that, rebuild with `dbt build --select stg_payments+`.\n\nI did not check the amount conversion, the reconciliation tests or the downstream numbers, because nothing downstream has run yet."}
